WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.278
Many businesses sell a lot and still lose money, because they don't know their costs.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:10.336
Variable costs change with how much you make, like ingredients and packaging.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.063
Fixed costs stay the same each month, like rent.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.584
Divide your costs by the number you make, to get the cost per item.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.733
Set a price above your cost, and check what others charge nearby.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:33.309
Before you move on, check: List your variable and fixed costs. Calculate cost per item. Compare with prices nearby. Set a price with a profit.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.513
In the next lesson: Record keeping.
